                  <msItem>
                     <title>Rupertus Tuitiensis, etc</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Two printed books bound together, the second
                        being Kaspar Sasger, Replica contra periculosa scripta (sl: sn,
                        1522).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Contemporary brown stamped leather over wooden
                        boards (which J. B. Oldham thought to be London work). Two clasps missing.
                        Pastedowns from a manuscript (England, s. xiii), with a well-drawn grotesque
                        in the lower margin of the page.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <physDesc> <typeDesc><p>Printed book.</p></typeDesc> </physDesc><history>
